  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31404392",
      "title": "Handling User Input in a Generic Way",
      "lectureOrder": 152,
      "videoOrder": 148,
      "sourceHash": "95fb053efce754a3e69fa3428ef5ba378412040bc5bd5256d7c61501bc18852f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 3.29,
          "en": "So let's now make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.29,
          "end": 6.163,
          "en": "we actually use those entered values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.14,
          "end": 10.11,
          "en": "Now this all starts in the input component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.11,
          "end": 12.98,
          "en": "where we accept the text input config,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.98,
          "end": 15.89,
          "en": "which allows us in the ExpensForm component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.89,
          "end": 19.03,
          "en": "to for example, add the onChangeText property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.03,
          "end": 22.1,
          "en": "which allows us to connect the inputs to functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.1,
          "end": 25.863,
          "en": "that will be executed whenever the entered values change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.9,
          "end": 29.78,
          "en": "And then we could use the ExpenseForm component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.78,
          "end": 32.083,
          "en": "to handle those entered values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.98,
          "end": 36.4,
          "en": "Now for that, we can start with a couple of state slices",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.4,
          "end": 40.48,
          "en": "by using useState, provided by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.48,
          "end": 42.25,
          "en": "and by then registering state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.25,
          "end": 45.42,
          "en": "for the different input values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.42,
          "end": 50.42,
          "en": "So here, we could then get our amountValue, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.44,
          "end": 55.27,
          "en": "And a function to update it, setAmountValue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.27,
          "end": 57.18,
          "en": "And initially it's an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.18,
          "end": 59.7,
          "en": "And that is important, I did mention it before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.7,
          "end": 60.72,
          "en": "in the course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.72,
          "end": 62.46,
          "en": "I wanna mention it here again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.46,
          "end": 65.16,
          "en": "whenever you fetch an input value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.16,
          "end": 66.94,
          "en": "you will get it as a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.94,
          "end": 69.27,
          "en": "even if the input provides a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.27,
          "end": 72.42,
          "en": "it is still some text technically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.42,
          "end": 74.67,
          "en": "So it's text that contains a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.67,
          "end": 77.33,
          "en": "therefore, if we talk about the data type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.33,
          "end": 79.19,
          "en": "it is a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.19,
          "end": 81.78,
          "en": "You can of course convert it to a number later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.78,
          "end": 83.34,
          "en": "to work with it as a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.34,
          "end": 85.02,
          "en": "but initially it's a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.02,
          "end": 87.07,
          "en": "That's why I said an empty string here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.07,
          "end": 90.45,
          "en": "as a default value for the amountValue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 90.45,
          "end": 92.49000000000001,
          "en": "And then here in the amountChangedHandler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 92.49000000000001,
          "end": 94.56,
          "en": "we can of course set the amount value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.56,
          "end": 96.72,
          "en": "to the text that was entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.72,
          "end": 99.753,
          "en": "which we conveniently get automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.75,
          "end": 102.99000000000001,
          "en": "React Native gives us the entered text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.99000000000001,
          "end": 104.5,
          "en": "or the entered amount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.5,
          "end": 106.983,
          "en": "if we connect this function to onChangeText,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 107.99000000000001,
          "end": 111.13,
          "en": "then React Native will make sure that this parameter value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.13,
          "end": 114.97999999999999,
          "en": "is provided automatically, and this will be the amount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 114.97999999999999,
          "end": 119.83,
          "en": "or the value in general, entered into the text input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 119.83,
          "end": 122.27,
          "en": "to which this function is connected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.27,
          "end": 126.03,
          "en": "So then we can update the amountValue in our state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.03,
          "end": 127.86,
          "en": "with the enteredAmount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.86,
          "end": 130.44,
          "en": "And we can also set up two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.44,
          "end": 132.82,
          "en": "so that we could change this from somewhere else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 132.82,
          "end": 135.1,
          "en": "in our component as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.1,
          "end": 138.25,
          "en": "and reflect the changed value in the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.25,
          "end": 140.67000000000002,
          "en": "by also adding the value property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 140.67000000000002,
          "end": 142.72,
          "en": "to the textInputConfig.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 142.72,
          "end": 145.07,
          "en": "So therefore, we add the value prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 145.07,
          "end": 147.49,
          "en": "to the text input component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 147.49,
          "end": 150.63,
          "en": "and by connecting this to amountValue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 150.63,
          "end": 153.57,
          "en": "Now, whenever we change the state, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 153.57,
          "end": 157.03,
          "en": "by pressing some reset button, which we don't have here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 157.03,
          "end": 158.38,
          "en": "but which we could add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 158.38,
          "end": 161.34,
          "en": "we also reflect that changed input state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 161.34,
          "end": 163.2,
          "en": "in the input component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 163.2,
          "end": 165.75,
          "en": "So that's how we could set up such two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 166.59,
          "end": 169.12,
          "en": "And now we're keeping track of the entered value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 169.12,
          "end": 172.84,
          "en": "and we then use that somewhere else in our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 172.84,
          "end": 175.7,
          "en": "For example, when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 175.7,
          "end": 178.32999999999998,
          "en": "Now before we deal with form submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 178.32999999999998,
          "end": 181.76,
          "en": "and with working with these state values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 181.76,
          "end": 185.45,
          "en": "we have a little problem to solve, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 185.45,
          "end": 188.41,
          "en": "And that problem is that we don't just have one input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 188.41,
          "end": 190.4,
          "en": "but multiple inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 190.4,
          "end": 193.58,
          "en": "Therefore, we might need multiple state slices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 193.58,
          "end": 195.37,
          "en": "which is no problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 195.37,
          "end": 198.67000000000002,
          "en": "but we also need multiple such handler functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 198.67000000000002,
          "end": 200.69,
          "en": "one for each input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 200.69,
          "end": 203.57,
          "en": "That's all the not necessarily a problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 203.57,
          "end": 206.38,
          "en": "but we can maybe find a solution that is a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 206.38,
          "end": 209.87,
          "en": "more elegant and scalable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 209.87,
          "end": 211.893,
          "en": "at least to a certain extent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 212.94,
          "end": 214.36,
          "en": "And therefore what I will do here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 214.36,
          "end": 215.96,
          "en": "which is not required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 215.96,
          "end": 217.78,
          "en": "but which I will do here to show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 217.78,
          "end": 219.93,
          "en": "that you could use this approach is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 219.93,
          "end": 223.04,
          "en": "I will move away from using multiple state slices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 223.04,
          "end": 224.67000000000002,
          "en": "one for every input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 224.67000000000002,
          "end": 229.15,
          "en": "to using one state slice that actually stores an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 229.15,
          "end": 231.74,
          "en": "And here, I will have my inputValues",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 234.9,
          "end": 237.713,
          "en": "and a setInputValues function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 238.56,
          "end": 241.77,
          "en": "And initially, I have three properties here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 241.77,
          "end": 244.12,
          "en": "that's amount which is an empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 244.12,
          "end": 247.95,
          "en": "date which is an empty string and also description",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 247.95,
          "end": 249.54,
          "en": "which is an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 249.54,
          "end": 251.593,
          "en": "So one property for each input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 252.63,
          "end": 255.52,
          "en": "And then I will make this function more generic as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 255.52,
          "end": 259.47,
          "en": "This will be the inputChangedHandler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 259.47,
          "end": 262.41,
          "en": "And I do expect to get the enteredValue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 262.41,
          "end": 266.15,
          "en": "because data is provided automatically by React Native.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 266.15,
          "end": 268.89,
          "en": "But I also expect to get another parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 268.89,
          "end": 271.65,
          "en": "which will be the first parameter we get here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 271.65,
          "end": 273.877,
          "en": "which is the inputIdentifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 276.36,
          "end": 278.7,
          "en": "And then my idea is that in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 278.7,
          "end": 280.82,
          "en": "I can call setInputValues",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 282.007,
          "end": 284.73,
          "en": "and update this state such that we keep",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 284.73,
          "end": 287.48,
          "en": "all the inputValues that haven't changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 287.48,
          "end": 290.51,
          "en": "but we overwrite the one value for the one input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 290.51,
          "end": 292.33,
          "en": "that has been changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 292.33,
          "end": 295.51,
          "en": "Therefore, since I will also need parts of the old state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 295.51,
          "end": 298.96,
          "en": "I wanna keep all the states that hasn't changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 298.96,
          "end": 302.47,
          "en": "I will pass a function to this state updating function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 302.47,
          "end": 304.5,
          "en": "following that best practice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 304.5,
          "end": 308.48,
          "en": "that if you update state based on the previous state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 308.48,
          "end": 312.26,
          "en": "you use this function form of the state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 312.26,
          "end": 317.26,
          "en": "And here we get the curInputValues object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 317.36,
          "end": 320.16,
          "en": "And we then return the updated object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 320.16,
          "end": 321.91,
          "en": "which is a new object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 321.91,
          "end": 324.273,
          "en": "where I spread all my curInputValues,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 325.55,
          "end": 328.52,
          "en": "but I then overwrite the one value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 328.52,
          "end": 330.85,
          "en": "for which we received a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 330.85,
          "end": 334.77,
          "en": "So the one input for which we received a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 334.77,
          "end": 337.59000000000003,
          "en": "And we should be able to identify this input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 337.59000000000003,
          "end": 340.2,
          "en": "by this inputIdentifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 340.2,
          "end": 342.13,
          "en": "And now the expectation is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 342.13,
          "end": 346.93,
          "en": "that inputIdentifier is amount, date, description,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 346.93,
          "end": 349.08,
          "en": "one of these three values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 349.08,
          "end": 352.58,
          "en": "So we can dynamically set this property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 352.58,
          "end": 354.68,
          "en": "and target a specific property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 354.68,
          "end": 356.45,
          "en": "by using square brackets here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 356.45,
          "end": 360.08,
          "en": "And passing inputIdentifier between the square brackets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 360.08,
          "end": 362.42,
          "en": "and then setting the enteredValue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 362.42,
          "end": 366.023,
          "en": "as a value for this dynamically access property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 366.88,
          "end": 370.26,
          "en": "In case this syntax doesn't tell you anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 370.26,
          "end": 372.48,
          "en": "this is standard JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 372.48,
          "end": 376.57,
          "en": "It allows us to set and target a property dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 376.57,
          "end": 380.45,
          "en": "Now, the property name we're setting is not inputIdentifier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 380.45,
          "end": 383.87,
          "en": "but the value stored in inputIdentifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 383.87,
          "end": 388.03,
          "en": "So if we receive an argument of amount,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 388.03,
          "end": 391.07,
          "en": "so a value for this argument of amount,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 391.07,
          "end": 395.13,
          "en": "we would target the amount property in this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
